[Debug] ----- Vuln Cause Analysis -----
The potential vulnerability is a Buffer Overflow. This vulnerability arises because the `congratulate_user` function writes a formatted string, including the `userName`, into a fixed-size `buffer` without adequately checking if the total length of the resulting string will exceed the `buffer_size`. If the combined length of "Congratulations, " and `userName` (plus the null terminator) is greater than `buffer_size`, data will be written past the allocated buffer, potentially corrupting adjacent memory or leading to a crash.

